**Test filters.** For this step these gates run only the tests their filter selects (plus any inherited expected-red tests); put the tests this step adds or changes where a filter value finds them:
- `constructor-unit-tests`: 
- `ui-smoke`: 
- `ui-tests`: `OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.FsxAcceptanceTests`, `OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.MaterialEditorWindowTests`, `OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.MaterialsControlsTests`, `OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.MaterialsWindowTests`, `OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.NkDispersionChartTests`, `OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.OutOfBandBadgeTests`

**How to implement.** A material's physics becomes a union that can hold more than the complexity tree, with one case for now, so that the next step adds the crystal case without touching every reader again (the S11.1 brief 'a new case beside the existing complexity tree'; .spec-md §3.2 'A material's physics is its complexity', which this widens). This is one step because the record field's type changes every consumer at once (the step 13 precedent). No behaviour changes. Each doc is one to three lines citing spec 0050 S11.1. (1) `OpticalConstructor.Domain/MaterialLibrary.fs`: directly after `MaterialComplexity` (`MaterialLibrary.fs:MaterialComplexity`), `MaterialPhysics` = `ComplexityPhysics of complexity : MaterialComplexity`, with `member this.toProperties : OpticalPropertiesWithDisp` answering the complexity's `toProperties`. `MaterialEntry` (`MaterialLibrary.fs:MaterialEntry`) replaces `complexity : MaterialComplexity` (step 13) with `physics : MaterialPhysics`, and its `properties` member is `this.physics.toProperties`; its doc says the physics is the entry's data and `properties` its engine composition. (2) The members the readers share, each with one arm here: in `LibraryFacets.fs`, beside `MaterialComplexity.anisotropy` (`LibraryFacets.fs:anisotropy`), `type MaterialPhysics with member this.anisotropy : Anisotropy`; in `MaterialComplexityEditor.fs`, beside `MaterialComplexity.isEditable` (`MaterialComplexityEditor.fs:isEditable`), `type MaterialPhysics with member this.editableComplexityOpt : MaterialComplexity option`, `Some` of the complexity when its `isEditable` holds and `None` otherwise (an option rather than a flag, ELEV012); in `OpticalConstructor.Ui/NkDispersionChart.fs`, beside `gyrationComponentsOfComplexity` (`NkDispersionChart.fs:gyrationComponentsOfComplexity`) and `MaterialComplexity.muKind`, `type MaterialPhysics with member this.gyrationComponents : GyrationComponent list` (the complexity's `gyrationComponentsOfComplexity`) and `member this.muKind : MuKind` (the complexity's `muKind`). (3) Readers. `MaterialStore.fs`: `MaterialEntry.versionPayload` (step 68) becomes `VersionPayload<MaterialPhysics, MaterialMetadata>` with `physics = this.physics`, so the version rule compares the physics structurally as it compared the complexity. `LibraryFacets.fs`: the private `constantEpsOpt`, `dispersiveEpsOpt`, `activeOpt` and `magneticOpt` match `entry.physics` (`ComplexityPhysics complexity` → today's body), the anisotropy facet extracts `entry.physics.anisotropy`, and the transparency facet matches `ComplexityPhysics _` around today's rule. `OutOfBandDiagnostic.fs`: `ReachableMaterial.ofEntry` (`OutOfBandDiagnostic.fs:ofEntry`) matches the physics, `ComplexityPhysics complexity` → `ReachableMaterial.definedSegmentsOf complexity`. `LibraryEntryFiles.fs` (step 25): `ofMaterialEntry` writes `MaterialPayload` of the physics' complexity and `toMaterialEntry` reads it back as `ComplexityPhysics`, so every entry file, catalogue file, snapshot and stored payload keeps its bytes and its hash (`BuiltInCatalogueParityTests` and `BuiltInCatalogueIntegrityTests` stay green unchanged). `OpticalConstructor.Storage/MaterialImport.fs` (`entryFromTabulated`, `entryOfAxis`) and `Report.fs` (`dtoToEntry`) build `physics = ComplexityPhysics …`. `OpticalConstructor.Ui/MaterialEditorView.fs`: `ViewOnlyMaterial of reason : ControlCaption * shown : MaterialComplexity` (step 13) carries `shown : MaterialPhysics`; `previewProperties`, `previewGyrationComponents` and `previewMuKind` read `shown.toProperties`, `shown.gyrationComponents` and `shown.muKind`; `initMaterialEditor` seeds through `entry.physics.editableComplexityOpt`: `Some complexity` → `ofComplexity` as today, its `Error e` giving `ViewOnlyMaterial (e.caption, entry.physics)`, and `None` → `ViewOnlyMaterial (ControlCaption "this entry's physics is not editable term data — view-only", entry.physics)`; `entryUnder` builds `physics = ComplexityPhysics complexity`. `MaterialsWindowView.fs`: `editableSelection` and the view panel's editability read `entry.physics.editableComplexityOpt` (`Some _` is editable), and both chart call sites read `shownEntry.physics.anisotropy`. `MaterialEditorWindow.fs`: its module doc names the physics. (4) Every test fixture that builds a `MaterialEntry` writes `physics = ComplexityPhysics c` for `complexity = c`, and every test read of `.complexity` reads the physics' complexity through a match; no assertion changes: in `OpticalConstructor.Tests` `MaterialProxyTests.fs`, `SampleProxyTests.fs`, `MaterialComplexityTests.fs`, `MaterialImportTests.fs`, `LibraryFacetsTests.fs`, `OutOfBandDiagnosticTests.fs`, `DispersionModelsTests.fs`, `ExportImportTests.fs`, `LibraryEntryFilesTests.fs`, `EntryFileJsonTests.fs`, `CatalogueImportProxyTests.fs`, `CatalogueImportInMemoryTests.fs` and `BuiltinCatalogue.fs`; in `OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests` `MaterialEditorWindowTests.fs`, `MaterialsWindowTests.fs`, `NkDispersionChartTests.fs`, `OutOfBandBadgeTests.fs`, `FsxAcceptanceTests.fs` and `MaterialsControlsTests.fs`, whichever of them build or read one. A comment or message in an edited file that names the entry's `complexity` field names its physics. No other type, member or option is added. (5) Tests. `MaterialComplexityTests`: `a complexity physics composes, classifies and offers its complexity as the complexity does`: for a constant isotropic complexity and a uniaxial dispersive one, `ComplexityPhysics` of each answers `toProperties.getProperties` at 600 nm equal to the complexity's, `anisotropy` equal to the complexity's, and `editableComplexityOpt` `Some` of it; a complexity whose active aspect is `PublishedLawRho LangasiteGyrationLaw` (step 10) answers `None`. `NkDispersionChartTests`: `a complexity physics charts the gyration components and the mu kind of its complexity`: for a uniaxial-active complexity the physics answers `gyrationComponentsOfComplexity` of it and its `muKind`. `MaterialEditorWindowTests`' `init seeds a new material, an existing editable entry, and a view-only entry` reads the view-only case's shown physics where it read its complexity, its assertions otherwise unchanged.

**Acceptance.** After the physics union lands, `MaterialEntry` MUST hold `physics : MaterialPhysics` with `properties` its `toProperties`, `MaterialPhysics` MUST hold the one case `ComplexityPhysics`, and every entry file MUST keep its bytes and hash; constructor-unit-tests MUST pass, including `a complexity physics composes, classifies and offers its complexity as the complexity does`, the count rising by 1; ui-smoke MUST pass; ui-tests MUST pass over the selected classes, including `a complexity physics charts the gyration components and the mu kind of its complexity` and the changed `init seeds a new material, an existing editable entry, and a view-only entry`, the count rising by 1; and build, elevation and the twenty s36 invariants MUST pass.
